          %title
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec \mathbb{Z}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topos"} étale topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X_{et})
            classifies are
            = succeed "." do
              %strong strict local rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} points of this topos
            are
            %em
              %span.newWikiWord
                strict Henselian rings
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/strict+Henselian+rings"} ?
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hakim"}> Hakim, III.2-4
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#Wraith"}> Wraith
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p We need to knead the definition of strict Henselian ring into being geometric.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \sum_{i=0}^{n} a_i x^i \in R[x]
            be a monic polynomial of degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            (so
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n = 1
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a field, a simple root of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(r) = 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p/(x-r))(r) \neq 0
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              More generally if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a ring, a
              %em simple root
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(r) = 0
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p'(r)
              invertible.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a field,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is
            %em unramifiable
            if in any field extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \subseteq Q
            in which we can write
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \prod_i (x-s_i)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i
            is a simple root.
          %p
            To make this definition work for more general rings, some work must be done. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R'
            be the ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[s_1, \cdots, s_n]/\langle a_k - \sigma_k(\vec s) \mid k \in \{0,\cdots,n\} \rangle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_k
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+symmetric+polynomial"} elementary symmetric polynomial
            %em hyperdiscriminant polynomial
            is the polynomial
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi p
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(p) = \prod_{i=1}^n (1 + p'(s_i) x) \in R'[x]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(p) \in R[x]
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              More generally if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a ring,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %em unramifiable
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(p)-1
              is nonconstant i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \langle \Delta_1(p), \cdots, \Delta_n(p) \rangle
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_i(p)
              is the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              coefficient of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(p)
          %p This is roughly justified by the following:
          .num_lemma
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a local ring and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1, \cdots, t_n \in R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1, \cdots, t_n
              is invertible iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \langle a_1, \cdots, a_n \rangle
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i
              are defined so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi i
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i=1}^n (1 + t_i x) = 1 + \sum_{i=1}^n a_i x^i
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i
              is a finite sum of a nonempty product of some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is in the ideal some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_j
              is invertible.
            %p
              Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_j
              is invertible, substituting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = -1/t_j
              gives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = \sum_{i=1}^n a_i (-1)\cdot(-1/t_j)^i
          %p This lets us arrive at our definition:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is
              %em separably closed
              iff whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a monic polynomial of positive degree, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is unramifiable,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              has a simple root.
            %p
              A
              %em strict local ring
              is a separably closed local ring.
          %h2#references References
          %p III.2-4 of
          %ul#Hakim
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monique+Hakim"}> Monique Hakim
              ,
              %em Topos annelés et schémas relatifs
          %p and
          %ul#Wraith
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Wraith"}> Gavin Wraith
              ,
              %em Generic Galois theory of local rings
          %p Section 21 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Blechschmidt"}> Ingo Blechschmidt
              ,
              %em Using the internal language of toposes in algebraic geometry
          %p
            includes discussion of what some similar topoi classify, including the étale topology over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S)
            partially via the internal language.
          %p
            See also
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/48690/what-does-an-etale-topos-classify"} this MO discussion
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/classifying+topos#StrictLocalRings"} classifying topos – For strict local rings
